Proof: Termux-native openjdk-21 successfully dlopened our Bionic-rebuilt
librlawt.so. The four-layer Bionic linker rejection observed against the
stock glibc-built librlawt.so in session 77 no longer applies — the NEEDED
sonames are Bionic-compatible (no .6 glibc suffix, no ld-linux-aarch64.so.1),
the VERNEED entry references libc.so with Bionic LIBC version (not GLIBC_X.Y),
and every undefined symbol is satisfied by Termux-resident .so files.

Key discovery — runtime:
  Java's -Djava.library.path is NOT honored by Bionic's dlopen when resolving
  NEEDED libs of a System.load()ed native lib. Must use LD_LIBRARY_PATH
  for the Termux lib dirs. (Java's path only covers System.loadLibrary
  lookup; NEEDED library resolution is Bionic linker territory.)

